--- body ---
## Context

DOIfetch v0.3.0 was tagged on 2026-11-10: annotated, unsigned tag `v0.3.0` (tag object d76db1f)
on merge commit 95efea63e1ba2f4d7d6c8a6f9176cb8e691dd808 of MinhHaDuong/DOIfetch, following the
author ruling of 2026-10-29 on unsigned release tags. Filed from the DOIfetch interface session
that cut the release.

Since v0.2.0 the release carries:
- the default output directory is `docs` instead of `papers` (DOIfetch ticket 0029, requested
  from a harness session);
- HAL is looked up by DOI first and its download passes the bot check (DOIfetch ticket 0028);
- text files are LF, pinned by `.gitattributes` (DOIfetch ticket 0030).

The harness still pins v0.2.0 in two places that are meant to move together:
- `scripts/doifetch.sh`: `DOIFETCH_REF=v0.2.0`;
- `pyproject.toml`, dev group: `doifetch @ git+https://github.com/MinhHaDuong/DOIfetch@fc85d31…`
  with the comment "Keep in step with scripts/doifetch.sh v0.2.0, resolved commit".
`STATE.md` also names the pinned tag `v0.2.0`.

Not urgent: `scripts/doifetch.sh` already names its staging folder on every fetch, so the
changed default does not alter what the zotero skill does. The HAL fix is the part the harness
gains.

## Request

Move both pins to v0.3.0 (tag in `scripts/doifetch.sh`, resolved commit 95efea6… in
`pyproject.toml`, lock refreshed), and the tag named in `STATE.md`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `scripts/doifetch.sh` and the `pyproject.toml` dev dependency name v0.3.0 and its commit
- [ ] The tests that exercise the DOIfetch wrapper pass on the new pin

## Plan (raid fc1083)

### Relevant files

- `scripts/doifetch.sh` — line 8: `DOIFETCH_REF` and its trailing comment (tag
  object and commit).
- `pyproject.toml` — dev group: the "Keep in step" comment and the resolved
  commit of the `doifetch` requirement.
- `uv.lock` — the `doifetch` package entry and its requirement line, nothing else.
- `STATE.md` — the DOIfetch line naming the pinned tag.

### Actions

1. `scripts/doifetch.sh`: `DOIFETCH_REF=v0.3.0`; the comment names the annotated
   unsigned tag d76db1f on 95efea6 and keeps the 2026-10-29 ruling.
2. `pyproject.toml`: the comment says v0.3.0; the requirement resolves to
   95efea63e1ba2f4d7d6c8a6f9176cb8e691dd808.
3. Refresh the lock for that package only (`uv lock --upgrade-package doifetch`,
   not a plain `uv lock`); `git diff --stat uv.lock` must show only the two
   doifetch entries (version 0.2.0 to 0.3.0, the commit twice). Upstream
   dependencies and extras are unchanged between the tags, so anything else
   moving in the lock is drift: revert it.
4. `STATE.md`: the pinned tag reads `v0.3.0`.
5. Not in scope, say so in the request: `OPEN_SOURCES` in
   `scripts/fulltext_cascade.py` keeps its six sources, so the harness's
   `--doi`/`--isbn` path does not use the CORE source v0.3.0 adds upstream; the
   file-name rebuild that helped HAL's search there stays, harmless.

### Test

- No new test: this is a pin move and no test may assert the pin's wording.
  Exit criterion 2 is shown by existing tests, run by name on the new pin:
  `tests/test_doifetch_helper.py`, `tests/test_fulltext_cascade.py`,
  `tests/test_fetch_receipt.py`, `tests/test_idh_lifecycle.py`.
- The tests that reach the real DOIfetch are `integration` tier (network, uvx):
  run them by name with `-m integration` and quote passed and skipped counts.
  The fast-tier ones stub the cascade and prove only the import surface.
- Evidence beyond the suite, quoted in the request: `scripts/doifetch.sh --version`
  answers `doifetch 0.3.0` (the tag resolves through uvx), and one real fetch by
  DOI through the wrapper into a scratch directory, as ticket 1344 recorded for
  v0.2.0.
- `make check` before the request.
